<title>JAPAN: Janome shares driven up by profit seekers.</title>
<headline>Janome shares driven up by profit seekers.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Janome Sewing Co Ltd were driven up in early Friday morning trade by participants seeking short-term profits, brokers said.</p>
<p>The shares were up 18 yen at 528 yen at 0037 GMT, with a trade volume of 3.831 million shares.  </p>
<p>The shares, which were at the top of the most heavily traded issues list, rose to 547 yen earlier in the morning.</p>
<p>Brokers said the shares were being bought by investors who want to lift the prices in order to take profits later on.</p>
</text>
